# oracle: fix lb/fluid Gaussian noise (D3Q15, trilinear stencil) on rigid molecules, one step (examples/PACKAGES/latboltz/microrheology/in.microrheology, cut down: dx 3.2, 1 step). The noise draws and the first coupling step agree with native to round-off; the noisy coupled run of 200 steps is in w132lb_microrheology.
# native: b332f28 built with -D PKG_LATBOLTZ=on -D PKG_MOLECULE=on -D PKG_RIGID=on (serial, 1 process; the installed lmp lacks LATBOLTZ)
# measured: thermo exact; per-atom 1.3e-11 (vy of atom 262). The Gaussian noise of the first step agrees with native; longer noisy runs are in w132lb_microrheology
# oracle-inputs: w132lb_microrheology.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           nano
dimension       3
boundary        p p p
atom_style      molecular
read_data       w132lb_microrheology.data
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    delay 0 every 1
neigh_modify    exclude type 2 2
neigh_modify    exclude type 2 1
comm_modify     cutoff 2.5
pair_style      lj/cut 5.88
pair_coeff      * * 0.0 0.0 5.88
pair_coeff      1 1 100.0 5.238484463 5.88
pair_modify     shift yes
mass            * 0.0002398
timestep        0.00025
group           ForceAtoms type 1
group           FluidAtoms type 2
fix             1 FluidAtoms lb/fluid 1 1.0 0.0009982071 dx 3.2 stencil 2 noise 300.0 2762
fix             2 FluidAtoms lb/viscous
fix             3 all rigid molecule
variable        x1 equal x[1]
variable        y1 equal y[1]
variable        z1 equal z[1]
variable        x2 equal x[242]
variable        y2 equal y[242]
variable        z2 equal z[242]
thermo_style    custom step v_x1 v_y1 v_z1 v_x2 v_y2 v_z2
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          1
run             1
